# Build output
dist/

# Dev
.astro/

# Deps
node_modules/

# Raw papers (not committed)
raw/

# Working records of the maintenance pipeline (local-only, not committed).
#
# These are the pipeline's own bookkeeping, not part of the knowledge base and not
# needed to build it: the wiki log, the rejected-resource list, and the concept
# screen that records which concept pages each ingested article enriched or
# deliberately declined. They stay on the machine that runs the scans, because the
# next scan reads them to know what has already been considered, and they are
# cumulative by nature, so committing them would put a running work log into the
# published history. `check-concept-screen.py` skips when the record is absent, so
# a fresh clone still passes the gates.
log.md
concept-screen.yaml

# Per-machine config overrides (host/port etc.) - never committed
wiki.config.local.yaml

# Obsidian
.obsidian/
*.base

# Python bytecode
__pycache__/
*.pyc

# Old Pico static site artifacts (removed, prevent recreation)
index.html
journal.html
search.html
tags.html
search_index.js
search_index.json
feed.xml
/pages/
# ...except the Sveltia CMS admin page, which is committed (needs index.html)
!public/admin/index.html
/tags/
# Permanent store for original source PDFs sent in chat (never committed)
pdf-sources/

# Sources that were NOT accepted into the knowledge base, and rejected resource candidates.
# Both list material that is deliberately not published here, so they stay local like raw/ and
# pdf-sources/. Keep them on disk; never commit them. `rejected-sources.yaml` is read by
# tooling/scripts/cron_prefetch.py so a rejected paper is not proposed to the scan again.
rejected-sources.yaml
rejected-sources.yaml.bak
resource-candidates.yaml
# weasyprint temp files left in the repo root by the PDF build
toPdfViaTempFile*

# arXiv client pacing state (one request per 3s, shared across processes)
.arxiv-rate/

# OpenAlex API key. Optional: the client falls back to the anonymous API without one.
# Never commit a key. See tooling/references/openalex.md for the ways to supply one.
.openalex.key
*openalex*.key
.env
.env.local

# OpenAlex client pacing/state (if ever added)
.openalex-state/
AIED-REJECTED.md

# Python bytecode (never shipped)
__pycache__/
*.pyc
